on.pack)."}},)LPROFILE",
  R"LPROFILE("additionalProperties":false}},"rules":{"type":"object","description":"Scoped settings and rules from what is said (R54): \"w tej rozmowie ustaw X=Y\", \"dla mnie zawsze pytaj przed depict\", \"for this conversation never run depict without asking\". `scopes`: the phrases that name a level of the scope chain (cut out of the text before the commands are read; none named = the default scope of the action_rules profile). `commands`: regexes matched against the folded text with the scope phrase blanked out; group order = `args`; `original` args are read from the text as typed, `resolve` args are action words turned into catalogue ids (an unknown word makes the input a message, nothing is guessed); `needs_scope`: only when a scope phrase was said (without it the plain settings patterns apply). The result is a proposal to run rules.set / rules.disable / rules.list.","required":["scopes","commands"],"properties":{"scopes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["scope","phrases"],"properties":{"scope":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"phrases":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1}}}},"additionalProperties":false}},"commands":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["id","action","regex","args"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"action":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"effect":{"type":"string"},"lang":{"type":"string"},"needs_scope":{"type":"boolean"},"regex":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"args":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"original":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"resolve":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"additionalProperties":false}},"action_words":{"type":"object","description":"Words (folded; a trailing * matches any continuation) that stand for exactly one action in a rule or a scoped statement (\"pytaj przed obrazem\": obraz* is depict, not a media action that is only planned). Tried before the phrases of the catalogue.","additionalProperties":{"type":"string","minLength":1}}},"additionalProperties":false},"phrases":{"type":"object","description":"The lexicon of commands next to the `phrases` of the catalogue's own actions: action id -> language -> phrases (a word ending in * is a prefix). Phrases the user's own conversations add live here (overlay profiles/intent_routing.pack); an action's own `phrases` stay where they are.","additionalProperties":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1}}}},"languages":{"type":"array","description":"Names of languages as people say them (folded, lower case; a trailing * is a prefix): what a phrase such as \"na niemiecki\" or \"into German\" may name. The value given to an action is label.en. An unknown name is never guessed.","items":{"type":"object","required":["code","label","names"],"properties":{"code":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"label":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"type":"string"}},"names":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1}}},"additionalProperties":false}},"arguments":{"type":"array","description":"Arguments from loose phrases. Each pattern fills the declared parameter `param` of the chosen action (an action that does not declare it is not touched; an argument already given is never overwritten). `regex` is matched against the folded, lower-cased text (Polish letters without diacritics); group 1 (and 2 ...) is read from the original text, so the user's own words are kept. kind text: the captured words, or `template` ({1}, {2} = groups); kind language: the captured word must be one of `languages`, else nothing is extracted. First match per parameter wins; patterns of the language of the input come first. A pattern with `action` is read for that action only (profile.set: the field and its value from \"work.projects=chess club\").","items":{"type":"object","required":["id","param","kind","regex"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"param":{"type":)LPROFILE",
  R"LPROFILE("string","minLength":1},"action":{"type":"string","description":"Only for this action (its id): a parameter name that several actions declare (slot, value) is read from the sentence for this action alone."},"lang":{"type":"string"},"kind":{"type":"string","enum":["text","language"]},"regex":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"template":{"type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":false}},"commands":{"type":"array","description":"Commands of everything the conversation can do besides the rules (P15, R54): a regex matched against the folded text; group order = `args`; `original` args are read from the text as typed; `set` fixes arguments; `element` is the element the command acts on ({id} | {resolve: current_conversation | last_message}; none = the application), `element_from_arg` leaves it to the action (settings); `takes_scope` lets the scope phrases of the rules cut out of the text and fill `scope`; `check_arg` keeps the command only when the text of that argument is itself a command (how do I ...). First match per list wins ties, the order is the order of the list.","items":{"type":"object","required":["id","action","regex","args"],"properties":{"id":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"action":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"lang":{"type":"string"},"regex":{"type":"string","minLength":1},"args":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"original":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"resolve":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"set":{"type":"object"},"element":{"type":"object"},"element_from_arg":{"type":"boolean"},"takes_scope":{"type":"boolean"},"check_arg":{"type":"string"},"graph_arg":{"type":"string","description":"M1-K0: the command is kept only when the text of this argument names a node of the graph projection (find_address); else the sentence stays a message („przejdź do rzeczy”)."},"graph_match":{"type":"string","enum":["exact","words"],"description":"How graph_arg is matched: exact (the whole name, an alias or the id, word by word with stems) or words (a name that has every word)."}},"additionalProperties":false}},"payload":{"type":"object","description":"Default element (actions.pack default_element: last_message, current_conversation): a sentence that names no element but brings its own text to work on is an ordinary message and the model does the job inline (\"przetłumacz na niemiecki: dzień dobry\"). payload_patterns: regexes matched against the text as typed (a colon followed by text, a second line, a quoted text). max_words: the content words allowed after the command (the words an argument pattern reads, such as \"na niemiecki\", and the filler words are not content); more is a payload. All numbers are calibration, not limits.","properties":{"payload_patterns":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1}},"max_words":{"type":"integer","minimum":0},"filler_words":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string","minLength":1}}},"additionalProperties":false},"conversation_language":{"type":"object","description":"When the words of an input show no language (\"undo\", \"ok\"), the answer is in the language of the conversation: that of its latest proposal, else of its latest message of the person that shows one. messages: how many of the latest messages are looked at; enabled false: the default language.","properties":{"enabled":{"type":"boolean"},"messages":{"type":"integer","minimum":1}},"additionalProperties":false},"context_modifiers":{"type":"object","description":"Short sentences that widen, narrow, deepen or flatten the context of the next turn, name a selector profile, or ask what was sent to the model (M1-D2 data; the router reads it since M1-K1b). status says so.","properties":{"status":{"type":"object"},"note":{"type":"object"},"permanent":{"type":"object","description":"Words that make a modifier a rule instead of a change for the next turn (\"na stałe\", \"permanently\"); default_scope: the level the rule is written at when the sentence names none."},"modifiers":{"type":"arra