"tasks.list"])LPROFILE",
  R"LPROFILE(}},{"key":"loom_usage_policy","scope":"config","group":"usage","type":"object","has_default":true,"description":"Usage policy options (growth factor, baselines). Raising expected consumption by an order of magnitude needs the user's confirmation; the confirmation is enforced by the usage-policy actions, not by the config write. P17: baseline_min_samples (preset 5): until a cohort has this many measured samples its baseline is the larger of the measured mean and a floor, so one short first message does not make the next ordinary one look like a tenfold growth (0 turns the floor off; a cohort with no sample keeps the old behaviour). baseline_floor_tokens (preset {input: 4000, output: 1000}): the size of an ordinary request the floor is derived from - input_tokens and output_tokens as they are, input_bytes as input x baseline_floor_chars_per_token (preset 4.0, the low end of the band the cost estimates use), cost_usd and money_usd priced with the model's price when the caller knows it. baseline_floor: explicit floors per resource that replace the derived ones (null = none). These are presets of what normal usage is, not limits; they are edited like the growth factor, with the same confirmation.","human":{"label":{"pl":"Bezpiecznik ×10 (wzrost zużycia)","en":"×10 fuse (consumption growth)"},"why":{"pl":"Jedyna reguła właściciela: skok spodziewanego zużycia o rząd wielkości wymaga Twojego potwierdzenia; tu są współczynnik i punkty odniesienia.","en":"The owner's one rule: a jump of expected consumption by an order of magnitude needs your confirmation; the factor and the baselines live here."},"effect":{"pl":"Zmiana tych wartości sama wymaga potwierdzenia; działania porównują szacunek z punktem odniesienia i pytają, gdy przekroczy współczynnik.","en":"Changing these values itself needs confirmation; actions compare an estimate with the baseline and ask when it exceeds the factor."},"levels":["person"],"group":"koszty","subgroup":"limity","flows":["actions.run","usage.spend","chat.send","use_model"],"summary":{"pointer":"/growth_factor","text":{"pl":"×{{v}} (wzrost zużycia potwierdzasz)","en":"×{{v}} (you confirm consumption growth)"}}}},{"key":"usage_spend_limits","scope":"config","group":"usage","type":"array","has_default":false,"description":"Your spending limits per period (the preset is none, so nothing is limited until you say so): a list of {period: day|week|month, amount, currency, on_exceed: confirm|deny|notify, rate?}. P18: every use of a model obeys them, not only action runs - a chat message, the routing model call, the background analysis, embeddings, media and an action's model call all go through the usage ledger, which adds the spend of the period (the cost the providers reported) and, when the caller knows the cost of the call, the estimate, and compares the sum with each limit. When one is passed, on_exceed decides: confirm holds the call with a receipt like the x10 hold (nothing is sent until you say yes), deny refuses it with the reason, notify lets it go and tells you. Importing a file or reading is never stopped by a limit. A plan shown in the conversation says beforehand that it would pass your limit. rate is USD per unit of the currency (an approximate preset is used when it is left out and the limit says so). Say it in the conversation: \"set a monthly limit of 20 PLN\", \"ustaw limit 20 zł na miesiąc\"; \"how much did I spend\" reads the limits back. It does not replace the x10 growth guard (loom_usage_policy). Runtime profile action_run (spend_limits). Default: none.","human":{"label":{"pl":"Limity wydatków","en":"Spending limits"},"why":{"pl":"Twoje własne progi na dzień, tydzień lub miesiąc; preset: brak, więc nic nie ogranicza, dopóki nie powiesz.","en":"Your own thresholds per day, week or month; preset: none, so nothing is limited until you say so."},"effect":{"pl":"Po przekroczeniu progu: pytanie, odmowa albo tylko powiadomienie — jak ustawisz; dotyczy każdego użycia modelu.","en":"Past a threshold: )LPROFILE",
  R"LPROFILE(a question, a refusal or only a notice — as you set it; covers every use of a model."},"levels":["person"],"group":"koszty","subgroup":"limity","flows":["usage.set_limit","usage.spend","chat.send","use_model"],"when_unset":{"pl":"bez limitu","en":"no limit"}}},{"key":"loom_zip_max_total_bytes","scope":"config","group":"safety","type":"integer","unit":"bytes","has_default":true,"description":"Most bytes one imported ZIP archive may expand to; the import is refused before writing past it (zip bomb guard). 0 = no limit.","human":{"label":{"pl":"Największy rozmiar po rozpakowaniu ZIP","en":"Largest unpacked ZIP size"},"why":{"pl":"Ochrona przed archiwum, które rozpakowuje się do gigantycznego rozmiaru (bomba zip); 0 = bez limitu.","en":"Protection from an archive that unpacks to a gigantic size (a zip bomb); 0 = no limit."},"effect":{"pl":"Import większego archiwum zostaje odrzucony przed zapisem, z powodem.","en":"An import of a larger archive is refused before anything is written, with the reason."},"levels":["person"],"group":"prywatnosc","subgroup":"bezpieczenstwo","flows":["import.file"]}},{"key":"loom_zip_max_ratio","scope":"config","group":"safety","type":"number","has_default":true,"description":"Largest uncompressed/compressed ratio of one ZIP entry; a larger one is refused while extracting. 0 = no limit.","human":{"label":{"pl":"Największy stopień kompresji wpisu ZIP","en":"Largest ZIP entry compression ratio"},"why":{"pl":"Wpis archiwum, który rozpakowuje się więcej niż tyle razy, jest podejrzany; 0 = bez limitu.","en":"An archive entry that unpacks more than this many times is suspect; 0 = no limit."},"effect":{"pl":"Taki wpis jest odrzucany przy rozpakowaniu, z powodem.","en":"Such an entry is refused while unpacking, with the reason."},"levels":["person"],"group":"prywatnosc","subgroup":"bezpieczenstwo","flows":["import.file"]}},{"key":"loom_git_allow_repo_config","scope":"config","group":"safety","type":"boolean","has_default":true,"descripti